{"duration_api_ms":232731,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"aa3697c0-7efa-46fb-a722-4e438700d259","total_cost_usd":1.8608738,"usage":{"input_tokens":56,"cache_creation_input_tokens":125566,"cache_read_input_tokens":2175909,"output_tokens":21047,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6730},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":125566,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1111,"cache_read_input_tokens":121928,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8927,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8927},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":56,"outputTokens":21047,"cacheReadInputTokens":2175909,"cacheCreationInputTokens":125566,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.8608738,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":6730,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_017R25f9uwWvDiVT2XRgryaQ","tool_input":{"command":"grep -v \"^/.*src/main\" /Users/christoph/.claude/projects/-Users-christoph-Privat-domain-centric-architecture-dca-ecommerce-sample-java/aa3697c0-7efa-46fb-a722-4e438700d259/tool-results/toolu_01VYRP6c8P1zt1pmeavp3cWT.txt | sed 's#/Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture/dca-ecommerce-sample-java/##' | grep \"^src/test\" | cut -c1-220","description":"Show test-source hits for payment-provider terms"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01BAFiEPc1qZSSBcRgQPCDPM","tool_input":{"command":"cd /Users/christoph/Privat/domain-centric-architecture && ls; ls dca-knowledge-catalog/bundle 2>/dev/null | head; ls dca-ecommerce-sample-java/.claude/skills/dca-knowledge/; cat dca-ecommerce-sample-java/.agents/dca/conventions.md 2>/dev/null | grep -i catalog","description":"Locate the knowledge catalog bundle"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":36,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the plan to `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/plan.md`. It replaces the earlier plan, which had stopped on decision `pay-through-the-provider-01`. That decision is now answered, and the new plan cites it. There's no `## needs-human`, so the story can go on to the test stage. I didn't run the plan gate (`story-gate.py --stage plan`) or any later stage.\n\n**Criteria and test levels**\n- `authorized-payment-moves-to-review` (happy path) is a Playwright **e2e** test. The suite's own shop now starts with a WireMock stub for the payment provider. The test asserts two things: the checkout lands on the review page, and the stub got exactly one `POST /payments` for the total the review page shows.\n- `refused-payment-stays-at-payment` and `slow-provider-counts-as-unavailable` are **integration** tests in `src/test-integration`. They drive the payment page through MockMvc against a WireMock stub answering `402` or after a 5-second delay. The shop gives up after the 2 seconds `project/tech.md` names.\n\n**What changes in the code**\n- **New REST adapter** in `checkout/adapter/outgoing/payment/`: it translates `201`, `402` and a timeout. It's only active when a provider address is configured; otherwise the existing stand-in takes the payment.\n- **Third payment outcome:** `PaymentResult` gets an *unavailable* outcome, which the use case turns into the existing `PaymentProviderUnavailableException`.\n- **Customer messages:** `PaymentPageController` shows the story's two exact messages.\n- **Other changes:**\n  - a `data-test` attribute on the review page's total, so the test can read it\n  - an updated `@ExternalUpstream` rationale in `checkout/package-info.java`, with the generated context map regenerated from it\n\n**Changed tests:** only `ShopUnderTest.java`, backed by decision -01. The gate treats it as a test file because of its name. Every other existing test keeps its expectations: the integration tests run without a provider address, so they still use the stand-in, and the browser checkout flows still reach the review page because the stub authorizes by default.\n\n**Findings (they don't block the story)**\n- Both context maps, and the rationale in `package-info.java`, still say \"a mock adapter in place of a real gateway\". After this story the stand-in is only the fallback.\n- `project/product.md` still calls payment \"a stand-in in the sample\", which becomes inexact once a provider address can be configured.\n- The checkout glossary says \"the provider's own reason travels through unchanged\", which the page no longer does. The document stage should fix these texts.\n\n**Open assumptions** (listed in the plan): the JSON field names, which `tech.md` leaves open; cancel and confirm calling nothing, since the contract has no endpoint for them; the adapter's provider id; and the happy-path test skipping when the suite runs against a shop started elsewhere.\n\nThe two knowledge-catalog nodes I relied on are both drafts: `/recipe/add-an-anti-corruption-layer.md` and `/decision/failure-channel-exception-or-result.md`.","ttft_ms":3165,"type":"result","duration_ms":234042,"uuid":"54071e08-7298-4cd7-ba8d-836546e80e9a","ttft_stream_ms":1876,"time_to_request_ms":52,"first_content_frame_ms":1876,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
